# This robot's settings for opendubs-arm@.service. Copy to /etc/opendubs/arm-service.env (per robot; a deploy does not overwrite it).
# systemd reads it as plain KEY=value lines: no `export`, no quotes needed, no variable expansion.

# Where the service runs from: nothing to set. The default is /opt/opendubs/arm, the bundle deploy-all.sh ships (software/openarm, description/openarm, sim in this repository's
# layout). Set OPENDUBS_REPO only to run from a checkout on a development robot; it must have that layout and be readable by kiosk.
#OPENDUBS_REPO=/path/to/opendubs

# The driver's config: a copy of software/openarm/gafro/hardware.example.yaml with this robot's CAN interfaces, directions and zeros, one per arm:
# /etc/opendubs/openarm-gafro-left.yaml and openarm-gafro-right.yaml, which the wrapper uses when OPENDUBS_ARM_CONFIG is not set. Each has the other
# arm's group on `bus: fake` (a service starts every group's driver). The model's servo gains (kp, kd) are used unless the file sets use_model_gains: false.
# Set OPENDUBS_ARM_CONFIG only to give every instance the same file, e.g. a one-arm robot's.
#OPENDUBS_ARM_CONFIG=/etc/opendubs/openarm-gafro-hardware.yaml

# The robot's stow pose (LEFT_STOW=.. / RIGHT_STOW=.., degrees): what `ctl park` goes to. This is where the service looks by default.
#OPENARM_STOW_CONF=/etc/opendubs/openarm-stow.conf

# More arguments for the service (e.g. a slower activate, or a simulator run of the unit).
#OPENDUBS_ARM_ARGS=--move-seconds 6
#OPENDUBS_ARM_ARGS=--backend mujoco --no-ros

# DDS is not set here: the wrapper and `arm` always use /etc/opendubs/fastdds-robot.xml (UDP over loopback, no shared memory; provision-ros.sh installs it) and the service refuses
# to start without it, because shared memory does not cross to another Unix user and a client in a person's shell would never get an answer. Lines here do not override it;
# OPENDUBS_DDS_PROFILE names another profile file.

# Only while the old stack's container is still around and a node in it must talk to this service over ROS: its DDS settings, as in
# opendubs-teleop.service.
#RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_fastrtps_cpp
#FASTDDS_DEFAULT_PROFILES_FILE=/etc/opendubs-fastdds-udp-only.xml
#FASTRTPS_DEFAULT_PROFILES_FILE=/etc/opendubs-fastdds-udp-only.xml

# Not here: the python and the gafro environment. They come from /opt/gafro/setup.bash (the venv, ROS 2, the library paths); OPENDUBS_GAFRO_SETUP
# and OPENDUBS_PYTHON change them.
